{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>He ties his ass to a vine.</b> He prophesied concerning the land of Judah that it would flow with wine like a spring, and the measure of the verse is that a man of Judah would tie one town to one vine, and load from a single vine; and likewise one she-ass would load from a single choice vine. And he said, ״he washes his garment in wine״ — a parable for the abundance of wine in his land." "<b>And according to</b> the view of Onkelos, the verse speaks of Israel and Jerusalem. ״אסרי לגפן״ — these are Israel; ״עירה״ — this is Jerusalem; ״ולשורקה״ — these are Israel, as it is said (Jeremiah 2:21): ״ואנכי נטעתיך שורק״. ״בני אתונו״ — its Targum is עמא יבנון היכליה; he translated בני from the sense of בנין (building), and translated אתונו from the sense of שער האיתון, which is written in Ezekiel (40). Or the verse may allude to King Messiah, and therefore it says ״עירה״ and says ״בני אתונו״, in the manner of what is written of him (Zechariah 9:9): ״ועל עיר בן אתונות״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "Ezekiel citation given only as (מ) in the source, apparently an abbreviation for chapter 40; resolved by reference to שער האיתון mentioned there."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:31.373803745Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}